// noUncheckedIndexedAccess, on for all of src.
//
// The flag is right — arr[i] really can be undefined — but turning it on for everything at once was
// 669 errors, and the way that gets dealt with in a hurry is several hundred ! assertions, which
// leaves the code exactly as safe as it was and makes the flag a lie about it. So it went on a
// directory at a time, each one's shapes fixed rather than asserted: src/shared, board/ink,
// studios/diagrams, src/main, voice, then the rest of the renderer.
//
// tsconfig.json is untouched, so `npm run typecheck` stayed green the whole way and nothing needed a
// @ts-expect-error (the repo has none). test/ is deliberately not here: its own 117 would be a lint
// gate only — the loader type-strips, so types are never consulted at runtime — and a test asserting
// on a value that is missing is a failing assertion with a stack trace, which is the point of it.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true
  },
  "include": ["src"]
}
